Only the OSS flavour was used as a reference. Nothing from the SkyTube Extra
flavour (YouTube Android Player API, Google Play services cast framework) is
included. The SkyTube application is not bundled, launched or required.

Files in this application that adapt SkyTube source, each carrying the
upstream notice, the GPL-3.0 terms and a description of the FitBaus changes:

    src/main/kotlin/com/fitbaus/bikebridge/host/youtube/YouTubeStreamSelector.kt
        from app/src/main/java/free/rm/skytube/app/StreamSelectionPolicy.java
    src/main/kotlin/com/fitbaus/bikebridge/host/youtube/NewPipeYouTubeCatalog.kt
        from .../businessobjects/YouTube/newpipe/NewPipeService.java,
             .../businessobjects/YouTube/newpipe/VideoPager.java,
             .../businessobjects/YouTube/NewPipeVideoBySearch.java
    src/main/kotlin/com/fitbaus/bikebridge/host/youtube/YouTubeMediaSources.kt
        from .../gui/businessobjects/DatasourceBuilder.java,
             .../gui/businessobjects/PlayerDataSource.java
    src/main/java/com/fitbaus/bikebridge/host/youtube/media/YoutubeHttpDataSource.java
        copied from .../gui/businessobjects/YoutubeHttpDataSource.java

Changes made by FitBaus (GPL-3.0 section 5(a)), summarised; each file states
its own changes in its header:
  - stream selection rewritten in Kotlin over plain descriptors, with an
    H.264/AAC preference, AV1 / high-bit-depth VP9 / surround audio rejected
    for the Android 5.1 console, combined streams preferred at equal height,
    a 720p ceiling, HLS for live streams and single codec fallback;
  - discovery limited to the default kiosk, search, paging and stream lookup,
    with FitBaus metadata mapping and failure classification;
  - media sources limited to YouTube progressive, OTF DASH, post-live DVR and
    HLS; the ExoPlayer disk cache, subtitles and SmoothStreaming removed;
    NewPipe manifest caches bounded to four entries;
  - YoutubeHttpDataSource: package renamed and the SkyTube DownloadUtils
    user-agent reference replaced by an identical local constant.

The YoutubeHttpDataSource class originates from NewPipe
(https://github.com/TeamNewPipe/NewPipe, GPL-3.0, Copyright the NewPipe
contributors) and is based on ExoPlayer's DefaultHttpDataSource,
Copyright (C) 2016 The Android Open Source Project, licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0 (licenses/Apache-2.0.txt).

